messages:
sahil: Heads-up — having a quick sync on client-visible status semantics. We keep seeing customers confused by mixed 503/429 responses when we route to degraded capacity.
jess: This has come up in sales calls too. Customers want a clear signal: is it a quota/limit or a transient capacity issue? :thinking: 
omar: Agree. Proposal: unify to a small set of surface buckets we show in the console + headers. e.g. `throttle`, `degraded`, `unavailable`. Each maps to an http status but we add a `x-rw-status` header with the bucket.
karen: UX ask: the console should show human-friendly labels, not raw codes. If we add `x-rw-status` we can map to tooltip copy. Can we craft copy for the three buckets?
sahil: Draft copy: `throttle` -> "usage limit reached, consider rate smoothing or contact sales"; `degraded` -> "service degraded, lower throughput or retry with jitter"; `unavailable` -> "temporarily unavailable, fallback enabled". Short and actionable.
jess: I like short + prescriptive. Also add quick hint for retry window for `degraded` if we can estimate (e.g., 200-600ms backoff).
omar: On server side we need deterministic mapping. Current behavior: 429 for quota, 503 when route falls back/firewall. That ambiguity is the problem. Let's add mapping rules in router: if cause == quota -> 429 + x-rw-status: throttle; else if fallback_active -> 503 + x-rw-status: degraded; else -> 503 + x-rw-status: unavailable.
sahil: Pseudocode I sketched: ```
if (isQuota(request)) {
  status = 429; header = 'throttle';
} else if (routeFallbacked(request)) {
  status = 503; header = 'degraded';
} else {
  status = 503; header = 'unavailable';
}
```
karen: Can we add a short machine-readable `retry-after-ms` header for `throttle` and `degraded` when we have a hint? Console can show it as "try again in ~Xs".
omar: We can emit `x-rw-retry-ms` when we can estimate. Perf/telemetry team: does this create noise?
rollout-bot: deploy started: feature/err-handshake -> canary on infra-qa (3 hosts)
sahil: Also need telemetry fields: `rw_status`, `rw_retry_ms`, `route_reason` in our traces. This will let ops distinguish real quota vs routing fallback.
jess: Product question: Do we want SDKs to surface `x-rw-status` as a typed enum so callers can program fallback logic?
omar: Yes. SDKs should expose `statusCategory` with values `THROTTLE`, `DEGRADED`, `UNAVAILABLE`. Add to SDK contract docs.
karen: I'll write tiny console copy and tooltip drafts if you confirm labels. Also will add a short runbook snippet for oncall: what to do for each bucket.
sahil: Runbook highlights: THROTTLE -> check tenant quotas, advise client to reduce burst; DEGRADED -> check current autoscale/alarm for node evictions; UNAVAILABLE -> broader outage playbook.
jess: One last ask: keep 4xx vs 5xx semantics intact for existing integrations. We should not flip 4xx to 5xx lightly. That said, the header gives clarity without breaking clients. :thumbsup: 
sahil: Good point. We'll rollout header-first. If any major partners object we'll provide a migration shim.
omar: Plan: 1) server mapping + telemetry (this week), 2) SDK surface + console tooltip (next week), 3) rollout canary -> beta -> GA with logs sampling.
karen: I'll add tooltip drafts to the console PR and ping legal for copy check.
rollout-bot: canary succeeded on infra-qa (3 hosts)
sahil: Nice. I'll open a small RFC doc after demo with the final mapping table and sample responses.
